// Spike fixture (s): an adjacent local CPU pair FOLLOWED by a post-pair call to an
// IMPORTED suspending function. The imported variant of fixture (q).
//
// Invariant this guards (deviation-judge #2 / code-reviewer, Slice-1 Round 2): the
// spike-host decision is made at TWO salsa query boundaries that must agree on the frame
// size. `frame_layouts_query` probes spike admission against the EFFECTIVE suspend set
// (local ∪ imported-suspending); `codegen_query` must probe against the SAME set. If
// codegen probed only the BARE local set (imports absent), it could ADMIT a host that
// frame_layouts sized sequentially — laying the frame out with the spike reserve but
// WITHOUT the imported callee's child sub-frame, under-allocating the heap block and
// corrupting it when the imported child writes at its layout offset.
//
// Current reachability (verified live, 2026-06-13): for THIS shape, typeck's
// `cpu_promotion_query` guard-probe rollback already DECLINES `entrypoint` — a CPU group
// plus a post-pair imported-suspending call makes a suspension guard fire once entrypoint
// becomes a state machine, so the promotion set is empty and no host is admitted at either
// boundary. The bare-vs-effective asymmetry is therefore MASKED today, not live corruption.
// The fix routes both boundaries through the effective set anyway, so the masking can never
// silently flip to corruption if a future slice relaxes the entrypoint-only gate or the
// guard-probe. This fixture pins: compiles, byte-identical both modes, clean run, and (via
// the codegen-crate test) entrypoint emits ZERO spawn calls + both boundaries agree.
//
// A LOCAL suspending callee (fixture q) declines in both boundaries because it's in the
// bare local set too; this fixture exercises the IMPORTED-only gap the fix closes.
//
// Arithmetic: fib(10)=55, fib(11)=89.
//
// Expected output (both modes — default and YNZ_NO_AUTO_PARALLEL=1):
//   55
//   89
import { ioWork } from `io_lib`

function fib(n: int) -> int {
  if (n < 2) {
    return n
  }
  return fib(n - 1) + fib(n - 2)
}

function entrypoint() -> nothing {
  let a = fib(10)
  let b = fib(11)
  wait ioWork()
  print(a)
  print(b)
}
